<!-- TROUBLE -->
<section style="padding: 80px 0">
<div class="wrap">
<p class="kick">Stay out of trouble</p>
<h2 class="h2">What can get a salesperson in trouble, and what Listing Accelerator never does</h2>
<p class="lead">One banned Facebook account, one wrong price or one customer file in the wrong place can cost you a lot more than a sale.</p>
<div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(340px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 40px">
<div class="card" style="display: flex; gap: 16px"><div class="ic" style="flex: none; background: #FDECEC; color: #B91C1C"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M5.6 5.6l12.8 12.8"></path></svg></div><div><p class="q">Bots that post for you</p><p class="cb">Programs that post or message on their own, or fake human typing to look like you, can get your Facebook account limited or shut down. <b>Ours never presses Post, Publish or Send.</b> You do.</p></div></div>
<div class="card" style="display: flex; gap: 16px"><div class="ic" style="flex: none; background: #FDECEC; color: #B91C1C"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 11a8 8 0 0 0-14.5-4.5L4 8"></path><path d="M4 4v4h4"></path><path d="M4 13a8 8 0 0 0 14.5 4.5L20 16"></path><path d="M20 20v-4h-4"></path></svg></div><div><p class="q">Delete-and-repost, and posting while you're away</p><p class="cb">Tools that delete and repost your cars every few days, or keep posting while you're away from the computer, are what dealers blame for Marketplace bans. <b>Ours never deletes, reposts or posts on its own.</b> Nothing happens unless you're there pressing the button.</p></div></div>
<div class="card" style="display: flex; gap: 16px"><div class="ic" style="flex: none; background: #FDECEC; color: #B91C1C"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3v18M17 7H9.5a3 3 0 0 0 0 6h5a3 3 0 0 1 0 6H6"></path></svg></div><div><p class="q">Wrong prices and sold cars still up</p><p class="cb">A customer drives in for a price you can't honor, or a car that's gone. <b>Every morning it checks each listing</b> against the store's website and tells you what to fix.</p></div></div>
<div class="card" style="display: flex; gap: 16px"><div class="ic" style="flex: none; background: #FDECEC; color: #B91C1C"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="5" y="11" width="14" height="10" rx="2"></rect><path d="M8 11V7a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v4"></path></svg></div><div><p class="q">Customer info on someone else's server</p><p class="cb">Most dealerships have strict rules about where customer information goes. <b>Ours stays on your computer</b> and your store's own OneDrive. Names and numbers are stripped before anything goes to AI.</p></div></div>
<div class="card" style="display: flex; gap: 16px"><div class="ic" style="flex: none; background: #FDECEC; color: #B91C1C"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="4" y="4" width="16" height="16" rx="2"></rect><path d="M8 9h8M8 13h8M8 17h5"></path></svg></div><div><p class="q">Credit apps and Social Security numbers</p><p class="cb">Collecting those in a side program is a big risk. <b>There are no SSN, date-of-birth or credit-app fields, ever.</b> That stays in the store's own systems.</p></div></div>
<div class="card" style="display: flex; gap: 16px"><div class="ic" style="flex: none; background: #FDECEC; color: #B91C1C"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 7h16M4 12h16M4 17h10"></path></svg></div><div><p class="q">Quoting payments your manager didn't OK</p><p class="cb">Payment numbers are the desk's call. <b>The Deal desk starts off</b> and only turns on with a manager PIN.</p></div></div>
<div class="card" style="display: flex; gap: 16px"><div class="ic" style="flex: none; background: #FDECEC; color: #B91C1C"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="6" width="18" height="12" rx="2"></rect><path d="M7 12h10"></path></svg></div><div><p class="q">License plates and copied ads</p><p class="cb">Posted plates can be a privacy problem, and five identical ads from one store look like spam. <b>Plate blur is built in,</b> and each salesperson's ad gets its own look.</p></div></div>
<div class="card" style="display: flex; gap: 16px"><div class="ic" style="flex: none; background: #FDECEC; color: #B91C1C"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 18V5l12-2v13"></path><circle cx="6" cy="18" r="3"></circle><circle cx="18" cy="16" r="3"></circle></svg></div><div><p class="q">Radio songs in your videos</p><p class="cb">Facebook mutes or pulls videos with copyrighted music. <b>The walkaround videos use a built-in music library</b> and warn you before you add a song of your own.</p></div></div>
<div class="card" style="display: flex; gap: 16px"><div class="ic" style="flex: none; background: #FDECEC; color: #B91C1C"><svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M21 12a8 8 0 0 1-12 7l-5 1 1-4a8 8 0 1 1 16-4z"></path><path d="M9 10h.01M15 10h.01"></path></svg></div><div><p class="q">Programs that read your chats</p><p class="cb">Tools that scroll, scrape or collect names on their own break Facebook's rules. <b>Ours never reads your chats or gathers names by itself.</b> You paste what you want saved.</p></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

